{
  "intent_version": "1.0",
  "part_name": "l_course_small",
  "primary_plane": "XY",
  "notes": "L-shaped corridor course, walls on inner + outer edges, open ends. Origin O = outer convex corner, +X = side B, +Y = side A, +Z up. Derived: strip_width = lane_width + 2*wall_thickness (full leg width incl. both walls); inner_off = lane_width + wall_thickness (offset of the inner wall from O). Build (all rectangles corner:origin): F001/F002 raise a solid L prism strip_width wide, wall_height tall (S1 leg A, S2 leg B). F003/F004 cut two origin-anchored blocks through-all (S3 = inner_off x seg_a_length, S4 = seg_b_length x inner_off), which leaves only the inner-wall L (thickness strip_width - inner_off = wall_thickness). F005/F006 add the full-footprint L floor slab floor_thickness thick (S5, S6). F007/F008 add the outer-wall L, wall_thickness wide, wall_height tall (S7, S8). Result: one solid body = L floor with an outer wall (X=0 / Y=0 edges) and an inner wall (offset inner_off), lane_width clear between them, open at both far ends. Valid only when strip_width < seg_a_length and strip_width < seg_b_length. All real lengths come from measurement-input.json.",
